A stage held back for a command's clip goes when the card stops following the turn.

Patch 0032 holds a stage that comes while a command's clip plays back, and
plays it at the next end. Only the next stage or the card's own resume of the
turn's stage cleared it, and the stage effect skips the ticks of a frozen or
sleeping card. A turn that ended while the page was hidden, under a lock or
while the pet slept so left the step's clip to play at the next end after the
turn, looping with nothing to stop it. The held stage now goes at a freeze,
when sleep starts and whenever the card puts the turn's stage back itself,
and an end plays it only while the turn is still on.

